Worldlens
================

This project is a TypeScript port of BlueMap.

BlueMap - https://github.com/BlueMap-Minecraft/BlueMap
Copyright (c) Blue (Lukas Rieger) <https://bluecolored.de>
Copyright (c) contributors
Licensed under the MIT License.

The code in this directory is derived from BlueMap at commit
e664c1abdf697c64703401dca1d7e1956f755f65 (see vendor/BlueMap), with legacy
Minecraft 1.12 support derived from BlueMap tag v0.10.3-mc1.12.

BlueMapAPI - https://github.com/BlueMap-Minecraft/BlueMapAPI
Copyright (c) Blue (Lukas Rieger) <https://bluecolored.de>
Licensed under the MIT License. The marker and API wire formats implemented
here are derived from BlueMapAPI at commit e20166d5ac93feab653392cf30a305a3e255754e.

Minecraft assets (block models, textures) are the property of Mojang AB.
They are NOT distributed with this project; the application downloads the
Minecraft client jar from Mojang's servers at runtime only after explicit
user consent, mirroring upstream BlueMap's "accept-download" flow.

Roboto - https://fonts.google.com/specimen/Roboto
Copyright 2011 The Roboto Project Authors
(https://github.com/googlefonts/roboto-classic)
Licensed under the SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1. Bundled locally (via
the @fontsource/roboto npm packaging, which ships it under that licence) so
the application loads no remote fonts.

Roboto Mono - https://fonts.google.com/specimen/Roboto+Mono
Copyright 2015 The Roboto Mono Project Authors
(https://github.com/googlefonts/robotomono)
Licensed under the SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1. Bundled locally (via
the @fontsource/roboto-mono npm packaging) so the application loads no remote
fonts. It is the first family named by every monospace surface: file paths,
config previews, engine logs, regex matches and keyboard keys.

TinyMCE - https://www.tiny.cloud/tinymce/
Copyright (c) Ephox Corporation DBA Tiny Technologies, Inc.
Version 8.11.0, offered under the GNU General Public License, version 2 or
later (or Tiny's commercial terms). This application is distributed under the
MIT licence, which is GPL-compatible, so TinyMCE is used under the GPL route
(license_key "gpl") and bundled locally from the npm package: there is no
Tiny Cloud script, API key or request to a Tiny host. It is the editor behind
every rich text field (see docs/rich-text-editor.md). The full licence text
ships with the package as license.md and notices.txt.

tinymce-i18n - https://github.com/mklkj/tinymce-i18n
Version 26.11.2. Community packaging of the TinyMCE language packs; its own
tooling is MIT and the language files carry TinyMCE's licence. Only the Hong Kong
Cantonese pack is imported, so the editor can show its interface in Cantonese
without fetching a file.
